		{
			"id": "Tx47iHOt",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 773.2247806837511,
			"y": 3186.2148244760556,
			"width": 890.998779296875,
			"height": 200,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "#fff9db",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b2k",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 919720190,
			"version": 445,
			"versionNonce": 1018246846,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783619955498,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Complexity for insert()\n- Time Complexity: * Worst Case: O(log N) — The new element is the absolute \n  smallest in the tree and has to swap its way through every level all the way to\n  the Root. The height of the tree is log N.\n    * Best Case: O(1) — The new element is larger than its parent, so the while \n      loop breaks immediately.\n- Space Complexity: O(1) — We only use a couple of integer variables  \n  (currentIndex, parentIndex), no matter how big the tree gets.",
			"rawText": "Complexity for insert()\n- Time Complexity: * Worst Case: O(log N) — The new element is the absolute \n  smallest in the tree and has to swap its way through every level all the way to \n  the Root. The height of the tree is log N.\n    * Best Case: O(1) — The new element is larger than its parent, so the while \n      loop breaks immediately.\n- Space Complexity: O(1) — We only use a couple of integer variables  \n  (currentIndex, parentIndex), no matter how big the tree gets.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": "8pC0VmWcfKu3GWEkM-U5q",
			"originalText": "Complexity for insert()\n- Time Complexity: * Worst Case: O(log N) — The new element is the absolute \n  smallest in the tree and has to swap its way through every level all the way to \n  the Root. The height of the tree is log N.\n    * Best Case: O(1) — The new element is larger than its parent, so the while \n      loop breaks immediately.\n- Space Complexity: O(1) — We only use a couple of integer variables  \n  (currentIndex, parentIndex), no matter how big the tree gets.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
		{
			"id": "nW7KNkWt",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 773.9781268466058,
			"y": 3425.171519198205,
			"width": 527.9993286132812,
			"height": 25,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "#fff5f5",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
