		{
			"id": "BzOaPNTK",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 777.3048801544375,
			"y": 3814.9812919459214,
			"width": 868.9989013671875,
			"height": 225,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "#fff5f5",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b4E",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1435520318,
			"version": 3544,
			"versionNonce": 109218082,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783620427422,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "3. Bubble-Down (Percolate-Down / Down-Heapify):\n- Compare the current node with BOTH of its children.\n- Find the SMALLER of the two children (for a Min-Heap).\n- If `Current Node > Smaller Child`: SWAP THEM.\n  (Why the smaller child? If you swap with the larger child, the smaller child \n   would still be smaller than the new parent, violating the Min-Heap rule!)\n- Repeat downward until either:\n   a) Current node is smaller than or equal to both children, OR\n   b) Current node reaches a Leaf position (no children left).",
			"rawText": "3. Bubble-Down (Percolate-Down / Down-Heapify):\n- Compare the current node with BOTH of its children.\n- Find the SMALLER of the two children (for a Min-Heap).\n- If `Current Node > Smaller Child`: SWAP THEM.\n  (Why the smaller child? If you swap with the larger child, the smaller child \n   would still be smaller than the new parent, violating the Min-Heap rule!)\n- Repeat downward until either:\n   a) Current node is smaller than or equal to both children, OR\n   b) Current node reaches a Leaf position (no children left).",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": "HoXuLwU4fJx5HNBR9wCHU",
			"originalText": "3. Bubble-Down (Percolate-Down / Down-Heapify):\n- Compare the current node with BOTH of its children.\n- Find the SMALLER of the two children (for a Min-Heap).\n- If `Current Node > Smaller Child`: SWAP THEM.\n  (Why the smaller child? If you swap with the larger child, the smaller child \n   would still be smaller than the new parent, violating the Min-Heap rule!)\n- Repeat downward until either:\n   a) Current node is smaller than or equal to both children, OR\n   b) Current node reaches a Leaf position (no children left).",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
